1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,380
With our already busy lives, finding time to exercise can feel like one more thing on our ‘to do’ list.
在本就忙碌的生活里，挤出时间运动仿佛成了待办清单上又一项负担。

2
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:14,820
So maybe it would help if there was ‘a best time’ to exercise?
那么，如果存在一个“最佳运动时间”，会不会让这件事变得更容易？

3
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:21,460
Could exercising at certain times help maximise our fitness goals?
在特定时间运动，能否帮助我们更高效地达成健身目标？

4
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:31,150
The answer is ‘yes’, but it’s easier than you think – no matter who you are, or when you like to work out.
答案是肯定的，但这件事比你想象的要简单——无论你是谁，无论你喜欢在什么时段锻炼。

5
00:00:31,150 --> 00:00:36,320
There are clear benefits to exercising in the morning.
早上运动有着显而易见的好处。

6
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:47,450
Many of us have more free time compared to later in the day, and it may therefore be easier for us to stick to a morning workout routine.
相比一天中的其他时段，我们很多人早上的空闲时间更多，因此也更容易坚持晨练的习惯。

7
00:00:47,450 --> 00:01:06,470
A study published in Medicine and Science in Sports and Exercise found that participants who exercised in the morning, increased their physical activity throughout the day, were less distracted by food, and slept better.
一项发表在《运动医学与科学》期刊上的研究发现，早上运动的参与者，在一天当中的身体活动量会有所增加，对食物的注意力会降低，睡眠质量也会更好。

8
00:01:06,470 --> 00:01:20,140
Exercising on an empty stomach before breakfast could also burn more fat and increase metabolism, which means you’ll continue to burn calories throughout the day.
早餐前空腹运动，还能燃烧更多脂肪并提升新陈代谢，这意味着你在一整天里都会持续消耗卡路里。

9
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:25,520
So, good news for early birds, but what if you’re not a morning person?
所以这对早起的人来说是个好消息，但如果你不习惯早起该怎么办呢？

10
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:32,620
Working out in the afternoon or evening also has benefits, just different ones.
下午或晚上运动有与上午运动不同的好处。

11
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:45,410
For example, your body’s ability to perform peaks in the afternoon, according to a 2010 study by the Scandinavian Journal of Medicine and Science in Sports.
例如，据《斯堪的纳维亚运动医学与科学期刊》2010年的一项研究显示，人体的运动表现能力在下午会达到峰值。

12
00:01:45,410 --> 00:01:59,810
Also, in the afternoon and evening, your reaction time is quickest, and your heart rate and blood pressure are lowest, which reduce your chance of injury while improving performance.
此外，在下午和晚上，人的反应速度最快，心率和血压也处于最低水平，这既能降低受伤风险，又能提升运动表现。

13
00:01:59,810 --> 00:02:06,350
But does any of this change depending on whether you’re a man or a woman?
但这些结论会因性别不同而有所变化吗？

14
00:02:06,350 --> 00:02:13,850
Our bodies are different, after all, so the best time to exercise may be different too.
毕竟男女的身体结构存在差异，那么运动的最佳时间或许也不尽相同。

15
00:02:13,850 --> 00:02:24,950
A 2022 study from Skidmore College, New York, looked at exactly this question and the results showed that there are some differences.
纽约斯基德莫尔学院2022年的一项研究就针对这个问题展开了调查，结果显示确实存在一些差异。

16
00:02:24,950 --> 00:02:36,980
Want to reduce your blood pressure and you’re a woman? Exercise in the morning. Want to improve your heart health and you’re a man? Evening is better for you.
如果你是女性，想要降低血压，那就选择早上运动；如果你是男性，想要改善心脏健康，晚上运动则更适合你。

17
00:02:36,980 --> 00:02:48,560
But, ultimately, the study found that there are clear benefits for both sexes to exercising at either time of day.
不过该研究最终也指出，无论男女，在一天中的任意时段运动，都能收获显著的益处。

18
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:51,640
So what time is best?
那么到底什么时间运动最好呢？

19
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:55,060
It seems the answer is: whatever time is best for you!
答案似乎是：最适合你的时间，就是最佳时间！
